WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.380
Galactic wars, festive cheer, and a very real&nbsp;
mission into outer space — this is everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.331
you need to know about the Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy's resident underdog.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:18.180
Cosmo the Spacedog's origins go all the way&nbsp;
back to 1957, over a decade before the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.620
iteration of Guardians of the Galaxy hit comic&nbsp;
book store shelves. During the Space Race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.300
Russia made history after adopting a&nbsp;
stray mongrel, whom they named Laika,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.560
to be one of their test subjects. In&nbsp;
November of that year, Laika was launched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.540
into space aboard the Sputnik 2 spacecraft,&nbsp;
becoming the first animal to orbit the Earth.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.320
Laika's voyage in outer space was&nbsp;
not one she would return from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.100
however — she died after overheating&nbsp;
during the journey. The incident has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.600
since become a talking point for animal&nbsp;
rights activists who protest animal testing.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.820
Despite her tragic end, Laika's&nbsp;
legacy lives on in modern-day media.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:59.160
Her fictionalized story was the subject of an&nbsp;
Eisner-winning graphic novel by Nick Abadzis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.660
while her name serves as the moniker for&nbsp;
the animation studio behind Coraline and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.820
The Missing Link. In addition, Laika's story&nbsp;
also happened to inspire two comic book writers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:15.180
Dan Abnett and Andy Lanning, who created the&nbsp;
character of Cosmo for Marvel Comics in 2008.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.620
Although Cosmo's first appearance in&nbsp;
the comics was alongside Richard Rider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.200
more commonly known as the superhero Nova,&nbsp;
Cosmo's backstory wasn't revealed until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.440
2008 comic book issue Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;
#1. Similar to Laika, Cosmo was a guinea pig&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.740
for the Soviet space program in the 1960s, though&nbsp;
their stories diverge when Cosmo is lost in orbit.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:43.140
At some point, Cosmo's entire being was&nbsp;
altered by cosmic radiation. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:48.240
he gained telekinetic powers. In addition to&nbsp;
being able to control objects with his mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.500
Cosmo also has the ability to speak&nbsp;
telepathically, which he uses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.200
communicate with various characters in person&nbsp;
and from far away. This is often used for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.900
comedic effect in the comics, as Cosmo's speech&nbsp;
is portrayed as broken, Russian-accented English.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:09.780
This space mutation also gives Cosmo an extended&nbsp;
lifespan compared to the average dog, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:15.180
a host of potent psychic powers. Luckily,&nbsp;
Cosmo tends to use these powers for good.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:21.420
Sometime after Cosmo acquires his powers, his&nbsp;
spacecraft drifts into Knowhere, which is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.940
severed head of a Celestial now serving as a kind&nbsp;
of planet in the Marvel universe. While Celestials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:32.700
didn't appear in the MCU in full form until the&nbsp;
2021 film Eternals, Knowhere made its debut in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.980
the first Guardians of the Galaxy film as the&nbsp;
home of Benicio del Toro's enigmatic Collector.

00:02:38.654 --> 00:02:41.181
"How wonderful to meet in the flesh."

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.080
In the comics, Knowhere becomes the place&nbsp;
of residence for Cosmo the Spacedog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:51.000
and Nova #8 reveals that he has become&nbsp;
the planet's chief of security. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.060
part of his job keeping a watchful&nbsp;
eye over the citizens of Knowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:59.160
Cosmo uses a brain stem from the dead&nbsp;
Celestial to power the Continuum Cortex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:04.500
a teleportation device for any location in&nbsp;
the universe. When Nova arrives, Knowhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.420
becomes a base of the Nova Corps, who allow the&nbsp;
Guardians of the Galaxy to set up shop there.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.460
Additionally, Cosmo's spacesuit is key to his&nbsp;
job of protecting the citizens of Knowhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:20.280
Cosmo stores a Dimensional Envelope in his collar,&nbsp;
a device that creates a pocket dimension in which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.480
he can safely hide the planet's inhabitants&nbsp;
in the event of an extraterrestrial attack.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.400
Cosmo's work as chief of security&nbsp;
for Knowhere eventually leads him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.600
to his first fateful meeting with the&nbsp;
Guardians of the Galaxy. Cosmo becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.200
an adamant ally of the team in the&nbsp;
2008 run of Guardians of the Galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:43.080
going so far as to suggest the team rename&nbsp;
themselves "The Retrievers" or "The K-Nine"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.640
in his honor. However, their meeting required&nbsp;
some happenstance on the part of the Guardians.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.980
Cosmo initially met Nova while he was on the&nbsp;
run from the Abyss, a cosmic entity that turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:58.560
humans into zombies. On Knowhere, Nova confronted&nbsp;
the Abyss with the help of Cosmo, who protected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.000
its citizens with the Dimensional Envelope in&nbsp;
his collar. Afterward, Nova recommended to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.440
Guardians that they take up Knowhere as their&nbsp;
new headquarters. At the time, the Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.920
of the Galaxy consisted of Peter Quill, Gamora,&nbsp;
Rocket Raccoon, Drax, Groot, and Adam Warlock.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.380
Cosmo eventually played a big role in The&nbsp;
Thanos Imperative, a comic book storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:26.040
also helmed by Cosmo's creators, Dan Abnett and&nbsp;
Andy Lanning. After invaders from Earth-10011&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:31.560
come to Earth-616, the Guardians team up with&nbsp;
Thanos to stop the threat posed by an alternate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.360
Lord Mar-Vell. The conflict eventually claims&nbsp;
the lives of many members of the Guardians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.600
including Adam Warlock, Drax, and Peter Quill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.100
the latter of whom charges Cosmo with&nbsp;
carrying on the legacy of the Guardians.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.920
In the Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.120
fans took notice of Cosmo's early&nbsp;
interactions with Rocket Raccoon.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:57.720
"Just concentrate, you stupid mutt… What?"

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.940
There's a little hostility between the two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.460
which will likely carry over to Guardians of&nbsp;
the Galaxy Vol. 3 — and this animosity also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:10.560
has origins in the Marvel Comics. In the first&nbsp;
issue of the 2008 Guardians of the Galaxy run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.400
the two exchange unpleasantries upon&nbsp;
the Guardians' return to Knowhere.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.040
Given that Rocket trusts pretty much nobody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.540
it makes sense that his relationship with&nbsp;
Cosmo is less than friendly. Nevertheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:25.440
the two eventually warm up to each other,&nbsp;
becoming reluctant teammates during Rocket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:31.140
Raccoon's solo comic series in 2014. In Rocket&nbsp;
Raccoon #6, Rocket goes through a lot of trouble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:36.480
to secure Cosmo dog treat cupcakes, which&nbsp;
Cosmo deems as crucial to his survival.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.460
As both Rocket and Cosmo are expected to&nbsp;
appear in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:45.900
you can expect the dynamic between the two&nbsp;
anthropomorphic Guardians will be explored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.640
more deeply. That's especially true considering&nbsp;
that the new film will, according to James Gunn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.900
delve into Rocket Raccoon's life and&nbsp;
origins. Since a confrontation with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:59.400
the High Evolutionary is on the horizon,&nbsp;
the humanity of anthropomorphized animals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:04.560
will likely play a big role in this third&nbsp;
chapter of the MCU's Guardians trilogy.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:10.080
Peter Quill's death at the end of "The Thanos&nbsp;
Imperative" storyline leads to a cataclysmic shift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.700
in the cosmic side of the Marvel Universe. Tasked&nbsp;
with carrying on the legacy of the Guardians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:20.160
Cosmo is responsible for bringing together some&nbsp;
of the strongest beings in the universe to fulfill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:26.640
Quill's original dream. This new team assembled by&nbsp;
Cosmo debuts in the 2011 mini-series Annihilators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:33.300
consisting of Beta Ray Bill, the Silver Surfer,&nbsp;
Ronan the Accuser, Quasar, Gladiator, and Ikon.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:39.180
Conflict soon arises between the assembled heroes&nbsp;
and anti-heroes, who are reluctant to carry out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:45.180
Quill's vision. Still, Cosmo is determined to keep&nbsp;
this group together. He offers them the mission of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.620
dealing with the Dire Wraiths, who have recently&nbsp;
broken out of their imprisonment in the Dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:55.560
Nebula. Cosmo doesn't reappear until Annihilators&nbsp;
#4 after the team has successfully dealt with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.700
the Dire Wraith threat, at which point they&nbsp;
return to Knowhere, ready for another mission.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.900
Of course, it speaks to Cosmo's influence&nbsp;
in the Marvel universe that he's able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.391
to gather a team that is so stacked&nbsp;
with powerful intergalactic warriors.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:14.580
Becoming the Nick Fury of the Annihilators&nbsp;
is far from the highest stakes Cosmo has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:19.140
been involved with in the comics. Cosmo's&nbsp;
creators, Dan Abnett and Andy Lanning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:23.580
also helmed the crossover storyline "War&nbsp;
of Kings," which revolves around a conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:28.440
between the Kree Empire and the Shi'ar. The war&nbsp;
not only draws in the Guardians of the Galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:34.200
but also the Nova Corps, Inhumans, and several&nbsp;
other cosmic armies. Cosmo's role in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.820
storyline gives him an opportunity to interact&nbsp;
with two underrated members of the Guardians.

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:43.980
After losing track of Peter Quill during a&nbsp;
fight, Mantis telepathically contacts Cosmo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:49.140
asking him to teleport them to Peter's location&nbsp;
with the Continuum Cortex. Cosmo later continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:54.060
to help Mantis and Moondragon, another notable&nbsp;
Marvel telepath, attempting to stop the war.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:58.980
However, when the space pirate Starjammers&nbsp;
bring the war to Knowhere, Cosmo is forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:03.960
to fight — one of the very few moments in&nbsp;
which Cosmo gets involved in the action.

00:08:04.849 --> 00:08:10.189
"I think I shall call him… Adam."

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:16.620
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3 features the&nbsp;
debut of Adam Warlock, an extremely powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:22.260
character in the Marvel universe. Warlock is&nbsp;
a humanoid android specifically crafted to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:27.600
the "perfect" human — and at one point, he comes&nbsp;
into conflict with Cosmo the Spacedog himself.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.880
In Guardians of the Galaxy #19, the Guardians&nbsp;
find themselves in a future ruled by Adam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:38.700
Warlock's villainous alter-ego, Magus. During&nbsp;
this issue, the Guardians become afflicted by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:44.280
trouble with the timelines, and Cosmo temporarily&nbsp;
becomes a puppy. They're later reverted back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:48.780
their normal forms by Kang the Conqueror,&nbsp;
but Cosmo doesn't last long after that.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:53.880
When Adam Warlock loses control of Magus and&nbsp;
ends up fighting the Guardians, he ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.880 --> 00:09:00.480
killing not only Cosmo but Gamora, Phyla-Vell,&nbsp;
and many other Guardians. Despite their losses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.500
Star-Lord suppresses Magus and kills&nbsp;
him before returning to Knowhere as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.240
a smaller team. Thankfully, the fallen are&nbsp;
revealed to be alive several issues later.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:14.820
Cosmo first appeared in live-action in the&nbsp;
2014 film Guardians of the Galaxy. Written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:19.200
and directed by James Gunn, the film is mainly&nbsp;
inspired by the 2008 iteration of the team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.000
which includes Peter Quill, Rocket Raccoon,&nbsp;
Groot, Gamora, and Drax. Guardians features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:29.640
an extended sequence on Knowhere, where Tivan&nbsp;
the Collector resides with his museum of cosmic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:34.800
memorabilia. One of those prized possessions&nbsp;
is none other than Cosmo the Spacedog.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.040
Cosmo plays basically no part&nbsp;
in the events on Knowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.060
as the Guardians attempt to sell the Power&nbsp;
Stone to the Collector before the arrival of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.900
Ronan the Accuser. The Collector doesn't&nbsp;
appear again until a post-credits scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:49.380
in which he is seen sitting with&nbsp;
Cosmo in the wreckage of his home.

00:09:49.546 --> 00:09:54.106
"What do you let it lick&nbsp;
you like that, for? Gross."

00:09:55.560 --> 00:10:01.740
Cosmo also made an appearance in Season 1&nbsp;
of What If…?, an animated series on Disney+&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.820
examining alternate timelines within&nbsp;
the Marvel Cinematic Universe's canon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.900
One of those timelines finds T'Challa&nbsp;
taking Peter Quill's place as Star-Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:13.620
facing off against a corrupted&nbsp;
Tivan. After T'Challa defeats him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.420
Cosmo is freed by the Collector's former&nbsp;
slave and taken in as a pet by Yondu.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:23.040
The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday&nbsp;
Special gives Cosmo an upgraded role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.460
with the current Guardians team. Early&nbsp;
in the special, it's revealed that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:30.240
Guardians have purchased Knowhere from the&nbsp;
Collector and are using it as a home base,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.920
which aligns with Knowhere's function in the&nbsp;
comics. Subsequently, Cosmo the Spacedog is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.820
now a de-facto member of the team, helping&nbsp;
them make touch-ups to their headquarters.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:43.440
Just like in the comics, Cosmo and Rocket&nbsp;
butt heads over their mundane work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:47.160
but this story takes a backseat&nbsp;
to Drax and Mantis' attempts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.844
save Peter Quill's Christmas. 

00:10:48.844 --> 00:10:52.680
Cosmo is voiced by Maria Bakalova&nbsp;
in both the Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:57.300
Holiday Special and Guardians of the&nbsp;
Galaxy Vol. 3, marking the first and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.560
only instance in which the Guardians'&nbsp;
space dog has been portrayed as female.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.820
Although fans have yet to see the&nbsp;
next chapter in the Guardians of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:10.560
Galaxy's adventures in the Marvel Cinematic&nbsp;
Universe, the end is certainly nigh. James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:15.180
Gunn has adequately prepared fans for the&nbsp;
heartbreaking final entry in the trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:19.740
implying that it will act as a send-off for&nbsp;
the current iteration of the Guardians team.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:24.420
Given that it's unlikely the entire team will&nbsp;
be killed off, some of the new characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:30.300
debuting in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3&nbsp;
may well become future Guardians in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:36.060
Cosmo and Adam Warlock, for example, may play&nbsp;
large roles in future films such as Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:41.400
Secret Wars or even the Nova project rumored to&nbsp;
be in the works at Marvel Studios. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:46.440
here's hoping for more adventures&nbsp;
starring Marvel's finest canine cosmonaut.

